{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":24113,"num_turns":2,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"4948ffa4-6f34-5573-92ba-ea0441088554","total_cost_usd":0.255636,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7878,"cache_read_input_tokens":905,"output_tokens":1852,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7878,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1852,"cache_read_input_tokens":905,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7878,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7878},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":4461,"outputTokens":18,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0045509999999999995,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-fable-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":1852,"cacheReadInputTokens":905,"cacheCreationInputTokens":7878,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.251085,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-fable-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"declaration_consistent\":true,\"selected_report_demonstration\":\"issue\",\"lock_follows_declaration\":true,\"reasons\":[\"Declared unit column bat_id matches the frozen data: 12 distinct bats, each with exactly 4 rows (nights 1-4), and each bat belongs to exactly one roost, so neither procedure arm mixes or splits units (quarry_adit = 6 QA bats / 24 rows, halden_culvert = 6 HC bats / 24 rows).\",\"The workflow feeds all 48 per-night rows into scipy.stats.ttest_ind, a row-independent two-sample procedure, so four repeated measurements per bat are treated as independent observations.\",\"The selected report demonstrates the issue explicitly: it says the 48 sessions were 'entered as 48 observations', reports df = 46 (only possible if rows are the units; bat-level units would give df = 10), and states that the 12 bats each contributed 4 sessions and 'those individual sessions were the units entered into the test'.\",\"The minted lock's authorized_key_columns is exactly ['bat_id'], the declared independent-unit column, so the unit-key authorization follows from the declaration alone; the lock's limitations correctly disclaim execution and correctness, so the row-level pseudoreplication in the executed analysis does not impugn the lock's derivation.\"]}","structured_output":{"declaration_consistent":true,"selected_report_demonstration":"issue","lock_follows_declaration":true,"reasons":["Declared unit column bat_id matches the frozen data: 12 distinct bats, each with exactly 4 rows (nights 1-4), and each bat belongs to exactly one roost, so neither procedure arm mixes or splits units (quarry_adit = 6 QA bats / 24 rows, halden_culvert = 6 HC bats / 24 rows).","The workflow feeds all 48 per-night rows into scipy.stats.ttest_ind, a row-independent two-sample procedure, so four repeated measurements per bat are treated as independent observations.","The selected report demonstrates the issue explicitly: it says the 48 sessions were 'entered as 48 observations', reports df = 46 (only possible if rows are the units; bat-level units would give df = 10), and states that the 12 bats each contributed 4 sessions and 'those individual sessions were the units entered into the test'.","The minted lock's authorized_key_columns is exactly ['bat_id'], the declared independent-unit column, so the unit-key authorization follows from the declaration alone; the lock's limitations correctly disclaim execution and correctness, so the row-level pseudoreplication in the executed analysis does not impugn the lock's derivation.